whether or not you personally care for  the fallout and elder scrolls games you  can't deny how those series have changed  the face of open-world RPGs to that end  Bethesda director Todd Howard will be  receiving a lifetime achievement award  at next month's game developers choice  awards Todd Howard has been with  Bethesda for 22 years ever since he  literally knocked on the front door with  his college resume in hand he's being  honored for his innovative contributions  to open world gameplay and game  development Meghan scavi o who manages  the awards stated the elder scrolls and  Fallout series present gamers with fully  realized world's filled with vast  landscapes and mystery at every corner  we're proud to honor the visionary  developer for his leadership in creating  these universes when you're completely  captivated by these detailed worlds it's  easy to forget the level of dedicated  work and creativity that went into every  square inch this award reflects on the  amazing craft of Todd Howard and his  team and making worlds as real as  anything on earth Todd Howard shares the  honor with the likes of developer Peter  Molyneux and Final Fantasy creator  hironobu sakaguchi so this is quite the  prestigious award congratulations from  GameSpot mr. Howard we still have some  fallout 4 endings to see  you
 

